{
 "_comment": "Curated Treasure Trails data for generate_clue_steps.py. npcFixes: clue NPC names the wiki tables give by place/role -> TCG card (null = not an NPC, no gate). noCard: wiki-linked things known to have no TCG card (so they are never gates; listed only to keep the validation report quiet). itemNameFixes: wiki page titles -> in-game item names where the catalog uses the in-game name. keepItems: item pages with no card that the old Sherlock 'items' list keeps (outfit pages). questAliases: wiki link titles -> quests.json keys. questAccess / partialQuestAccess: a region's gate quest -> access_routes.json key; when a step needs that quest (complete / started) the generator records the access key instead, because the access routes already hold the quest plus the other ways in (e.g. fairy ring CKS for Morytania). itemGroups: wiki link titles for 'any X' / set wordings -> slots (each slot: cards + mode 'any'|'all'; 'sets' = any one complete set). linkGroups: wiki link titles that map to a shared requirement list (group = REQ_GROUPS key in preview.html, tool = TOOL_TIERS key). locationRules: regex (case-insensitive) on a step's location text -> access keys / quests / partialQuests; replaces _CLUE_QUEST_LOCKS in preview.html. hotcoldRegions: Hot/Cold Master page region headers -> access key, with per-location exceptions. emoteUnlocks: emotes that must be unlocked first. sherlockOverrides / emoteOverrides / coordinateOverrides / crypticOverrides / talkOverrides (anagram+cipher, by NPC): hand-fixed slots/requirements for rows the parser can't read (keyed by task text, clue text prefix or coordinate shorthand). Checked against the OSRS Wiki 2026-10-11.",
